verage low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.19\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.12 to +0.26), about +2.5\u00b0F since 1892. Kalamazoo's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.14\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.05 to +0.23), about +1.9\u00b0F since 1892.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in 7 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Kalamazoo's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.14 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 33.8 inches a year. The wettest year was 1975 (46.90 in); the driest, 1953 (20.83 in). Kalamazoo almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is nan inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}